  "argument": "The claim of non-alignment between the extraction thresholds and the declared performance bars is statistically supported by the stark failure rate, but the underlying quantitative framework is highly compromised. With a sample size of only N=18, any statistical estimation of the true extraction performance has extremely low power and wide confidence intervals. The analysis suffers from structural data defects, such as a storm with an impossible catalogue radius of exactly 0.00 and frames missing feature extractions entirely, which confound the performance metrics. Furthermore, Condition 2 on the raw path was never pre-registered or previously computed, rendering it a post-hoc metric evaluated without multiplicity corrections. Although the binomial probability of achieving 3 or fewer successes out of 18 under a null target of 50% (9 of 18) is small (p = 0.0037), confirming the failure to meet the bar, the overall statistical quality of this pipeline is too weak to support any robust positive inferences.",
