  "argument": "The causal attribution of the performance deficit to threshold extraction mechanics is heavily confounded. First, spatial look-ahead in the SWT pipeline may artificially inflate its performance relative to the raw pass, meaning the delta is driven by information leakage rather than extraction robustness. Second, physical characteristics of the storms act as shared drivers: weaker or smaller systems naturally lead to smaller catalogue radii (including invalid 0.00 values) and simultaneously make features harder to extract. Finally, selection effects from arbitrary dateline exclusions prevent establishing a clean causal relationship. Without isolating these confounding factors, the observed numerical differences cannot be causally attributed to the extraction thresholds themselves.",
